From: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: allow disabling automatic shared GPIO ownership

The downstream Spectra resource manager arbitrates shared camera GPIOs
through the legacy integer API. Reserving those lines for GPIO proxies
makes every sensor power-up fail with EBUSY before Spectra can acquire
them.

Expose the existing setting to expert configurations so vamOS can retain
Spectra's GPIO ownership. Keep automatic sharing enabled by default.

Signed-off-by: Andrei Radulescu <andi.radulescu@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpio/Kconfig | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
--- a/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/gpio/Kconfig
@@ -46,9 +46,15 @@ config GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP
 	bool
 
 config GPIO_SHARED
-	def_bool y
+	bool "Automatic shared GPIO ownership" if EXPERT
+	default y
 	depends on HAVE_SHARED_GPIOS || COMPILE_TEST
 	select AUXILIARY_BUS
+	help
+	  Automatically reserve GPIOs referenced by multiple firmware consumers
+	  and arbitrate their values through shared GPIO proxies. Disable this
+	  when legacy GPIO consumers already manage ownership of shared lines.
+	  If unsure, say Y.
 
 config DEBUG_GPIO
 	bool "Debug GPIO calls"
